# DineAI — Menu Intelligence Framework Evolution

## Goal

Evolve DineAI from a "Recipe Framework" into a complete **Restaurant Menu
Intelligence Framework**.  The system must become fully data-driven:
a restaurant uploads its CSV, and the framework automatically detects
capabilities, configures all pipeline stages, and becomes production-ready
— without any code modifications.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1 — `app.py` modification scope**
> The dynamic ranking (requirement 4) and dynamic filtering (requirement 5)
> are most cleanly solved by making the underlying `ranking.py` and
> `filtering.py` modules self-detecting.  This avoids touching `app.py`.
> The `RankingStage` in `app.py` hardcodes Rating+Price+Semantic — but if
> `WeightedRankingStrategy` internally filters unavailable factors and
> redistributes weights, the stage works without modification.
> **Confirmed approach: do NOT modify app.py.**

> [!NOTE]
> **Q2 — Canonical column name**
> The internal canonical name will remain `recipe_name` to avoid breaking
> the existing adapter chain, but the `AliasRegistry` will be expanded so
> that `menu_item_name`, `menu_item`, `item`, `product_name` all resolve to it.
> Externally the framework refers to this concept as "Menu Item".

